1
00:00:00,935 --> 00:00:03,770
♪ In the not too distant future

2
00:00:03,803 --> 00:00:06,940
♪ Somewhere in time and space

3
00:00:06,973 --> 00:00:10,010
♪ Mike Nelson and his robot pals

4
00:00:10,043 --> 00:00:13,180
♪ Are caught in an endless chase

5
00:00:13,213 --> 00:00:16,183
♪ Pursued by a woman
whose name is Pearl

6
00:00:16,217 --> 00:00:19,353
♪ An evil gal who
wants to rule the world

7
00:00:19,387 --> 00:00:22,088
♪ She threw a few
things in her purse

8
00:00:22,122 --> 00:00:23,925
♪ And in a rocket
ship she hunts him

9
00:00:23,958 --> 00:00:25,960
♪ All across the universe

10
00:00:25,993 --> 00:00:28,762
I'll get you!

11
00:00:28,795 --> 00:00:31,765
♪ I'll send him cheesy movies

12
00:00:31,798 --> 00:00:34,135
♪ The worst I can find

13
00:00:34,168 --> 00:00:35,335
♪ La-la-la

14
00:00:35,368 --> 00:00:37,805
♪ He'll have to sit
and watch them all

15
00:00:37,838 --> 00:00:40,575
♪ And I'll monitor his mind

16
00:00:40,608 --> 00:00:41,642
♪ La-la-la

17
00:00:41,675 --> 00:00:43,977
♪ Now keep in mind
Mike can't control

18
00:00:44,010 --> 00:00:46,813
♪ Where the movies begin or end

19
00:00:46,847 --> 00:00:47,848
♪ La-la-la

20
00:00:47,882 --> 00:00:50,183
♪ He'll try to keep his sanity

21
00:00:50,217 --> 00:00:54,388
♪ With the help of
his robot friends

22
00:00:55,490 --> 00:00:56,890
Robot roll call.

23
00:00:56,923 --> 00:00:58,625
- Cambot.
- You're on.

24
00:00:58,658 --> 00:00:59,893
- Gypsy.
- Oh my stars.

25
00:00:59,927 --> 00:01:01,328
- Tom Servo.
- Check me out.

26
00:01:01,362 --> 00:01:02,563
- Crow.
- I’m different.

27
00:01:02,597 --> 00:01:06,100
♪ If you're wondering
how he eats and breathes

28
00:01:06,133 --> 00:01:08,635
♪ And other science facts

29
00:01:08,668 --> 00:01:09,637
♪ La-la-la

30
00:01:09,670 --> 00:01:12,138
♪ Just repeat to
yourself, it's just a show

31
00:01:12,172 --> 00:01:15,275
♪ I should really just relax

32
00:01:15,308 --> 00:01:20,515
♪ For Mystery Science
Theater 3000

33
00:01:22,483 --> 00:01:27,655
(rumbling, clicking and beeping)

34
00:01:33,862 --> 00:01:35,497
Help!

35
00:01:35,530 --> 00:01:36,997
Help!

36
00:01:37,030 --> 00:01:38,232
Crow, what is it?

37
00:01:38,265 --> 00:01:39,633
Hey Mike, give me
a hand here will you?

38
00:01:39,667 --> 00:01:42,268
I'm having a real problem
with my Thighmaster.

39
00:01:42,302 --> 00:01:43,870
Probably should have
looked at the directions

40
00:01:43,903 --> 00:01:46,273
before I started
messing with it, but no,

41
00:01:46,307 --> 00:01:49,142
I just had to work
on my trouble spots.

42
00:01:49,175 --> 00:01:51,612
Hey Crow, did you know
this was a Thaw Master?

43
00:01:51,645 --> 00:01:53,713
What? A Thaw Master?

44
00:01:53,747 --> 00:01:57,050
Well, how do you like
that? (laughs falsely)

45
00:01:57,083 --> 00:01:58,485
Hi Mike, hi Crow.

46
00:01:58,518 --> 00:01:59,953
Say guys, breakfast is
going to be a little late.

47
00:01:59,987 --> 00:02:01,588
This pot roast just
won't thaw yet.

48
00:02:01,622 --> 00:02:03,290
There's something wrong
with the Thaw Master.

49
00:02:03,323 --> 00:02:05,625
No Servo, this
is a Thighmaster.

50
00:02:05,658 --> 00:02:07,762
(laughs) A Thighmaster?
Well, no wonder.

51
00:02:07,795 --> 00:02:09,097
(all laugh sarcastically)

52
00:02:09,130 --> 00:02:10,263
This is never going to thaw.

53
00:02:10,297 --> 00:02:11,565
We'll be right back.

54
00:02:11,598 --> 00:02:13,667
- Son of a gun.
- That's good.

55
00:02:13,700 --> 00:02:18,438
(light music)

56
00:02:19,540 --> 00:02:22,075
(laughs) Thaw
Master, Thighmaster.

57
00:02:22,108 --> 00:02:24,210
Thighmaster, Thaw Master.

58
00:02:24,243 --> 00:02:25,945
Reminds me of that
time I tried to wear

59
00:02:25,978 --> 00:02:28,015
that hand hammered
wok for underpants.

60
00:02:28,048 --> 00:02:29,082
Yeah, that really...

61
00:02:29,115 --> 00:02:31,918
Hey, Mrs.. Forrester's calling.

62
00:02:31,952 --> 00:02:33,687
We'll begin
with a frontal cut.

63
00:02:33,720 --> 00:02:35,655
- But has he been washed?
- I washed him earlier.

64
00:02:35,688 --> 00:02:37,623
With my mind.
It was not pleasant.

65
00:02:37,657 --> 00:02:41,595
Hi, guys. Things have
deteriorated down here.

66
00:02:41,628 --> 00:02:43,463
Unless I'm mistaken,
and frankly,

67
00:02:43,497 --> 00:02:44,665
what are the odds of that?

68
00:02:44,698 --> 00:02:47,768
The brain guys are
about to dissect Bobo.

69
00:02:47,802 --> 00:02:49,435
Say, could we get on
with this dissection?

70
00:02:49,468 --> 00:02:53,507
- I think it's almost mealtime.
- Bobo's very stupid.

71
00:02:53,540 --> 00:02:56,277
Anyway, I'm locked in
some kind of force-field.

72
00:02:56,310 --> 00:02:58,912
(electronic sounds)

73
00:02:58,945 --> 00:03:00,747
So here's the deal.

74
00:03:00,780 --> 00:03:03,917
I know you guys despise
me, even loathe me.

75
00:03:03,950 --> 00:03:05,753
So could you help me out?

76
00:03:05,787 --> 00:03:06,687
Careful. Careful.

77
00:03:06,720 --> 00:03:08,888
I need a distraction
of some kind.

78
00:03:08,922 --> 00:03:10,123
If you can think of something,

79
00:03:10,157 --> 00:03:12,660
I promise to never show you

80
00:03:12,693 --> 00:03:15,530
another bad movie again.

81
00:03:15,563 --> 00:03:16,663
Really.

82
00:03:16,697 --> 00:03:17,598
Never again, ever.

83
00:03:17,632 --> 00:03:19,267
Hmm, you think
we can trust her?

84
00:03:19,300 --> 00:03:20,968
I don't know.

85
00:03:21,002 --> 00:03:23,003
(pleadingly) Pwease?

86
00:03:23,037 --> 00:03:26,473
Pwease, pwetty
pwease, for Pearl?

87
00:03:26,507 --> 00:03:30,110
Pearl needs a distraction
so bad. Pwease?

88
00:03:30,143 --> 00:03:33,147
Come on. For Pearl.

89
00:03:33,180 --> 00:03:34,548
Pwease?

90
00:03:34,582 --> 00:03:36,617
(Crow retches)
My god, stop it.

91
00:03:36,650 --> 00:03:38,852
Okay, fine, fine.
Just don't do that.

92
00:03:38,885 --> 00:03:41,555
Maybe the nanites have an idea.

93
00:03:41,588 --> 00:03:44,658
Hello nanites, could you
create a distraction?

94
00:03:44,692 --> 00:03:45,492
A distraction? Cool.

95
00:03:45,525 --> 00:03:46,960
I know, I know, I know.

96
00:03:46,993 --> 00:03:48,795
We can send a fleet of tiny
ships down there to pants them.

97
00:03:48,828 --> 00:03:50,263
(nanite laughs)
Well, gee, that seems

98
00:03:50,297 --> 00:03:52,132
- kind of complicated.
- Oh, I know.

99
00:03:52,165 --> 00:03:53,467
Simpler. Sure, okay.

100
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:55,702
I know, we could always
biosynthesize an android

101
00:03:55,735 --> 00:03:57,703
and send down there to say,
"Hey, look over there."

102
00:03:57,737 --> 00:03:59,205
(nanite laughs)
(Mike laughs falsely) Great.

103
00:03:59,238 --> 00:04:00,975
Why don't you just
cut the tractor beam

104
00:04:01,008 --> 00:04:02,308
that's holding us here?

105
00:04:02,342 --> 00:04:03,943
Ah, fine, a
number three, sure.

106
00:04:03,977 --> 00:04:05,512
We never get to
do anything fun.

107
00:04:05,545 --> 00:04:07,113
(pulsing)
There. It's done.

108
00:04:07,147 --> 00:04:08,515
Whoa. Hey, great.

109
00:04:08,548 --> 00:04:10,750
How's that, Mrs. Forrester?
Is that distracting?

110
00:04:10,783 --> 00:04:13,620
- What the devil was that?
- Very distracting.

111
00:04:13,653 --> 00:04:15,957
- Yes.
- Observer, you remain here.

112
00:04:15,990 --> 00:04:17,925
And I will check it out.

113
00:04:17,958 --> 00:04:19,593
- Certainly.
- Guard.

114
00:04:19,627 --> 00:04:22,695
Hey, guard. I got
a sick man in here.

115
00:04:22,728 --> 00:04:24,030
Do you mean me?
Because I'm not sick.

116
00:04:24,063 --> 00:04:25,665
- I’m being dissected.
- Shut up.

117
00:04:25,698 --> 00:04:27,633
- Okay.
- Your friend Observer

118
00:04:27,667 --> 00:04:29,937
created an invisible
man with his mind

119
00:04:29,970 --> 00:04:31,872
and put him in here with me.

120
00:04:31,905 --> 00:04:33,173
I suppose that's possible--

121
00:04:33,207 --> 00:04:36,210
Yeah, and now he's
looking real sick.

122
00:04:36,243 --> 00:04:37,677
Uh-oh, you better
get in here quick.

123
00:04:37,710 --> 00:04:39,780
I don't think you'd
want him to die.

124
00:04:39,813 --> 00:04:40,982
Well, where is here?

125
00:04:41,015 --> 00:04:42,983
He's right over there. Look.

126
00:04:43,017 --> 00:04:44,818
Oh boy, he sure looks bad.

127
00:04:44,852 --> 00:04:45,985
I'm sorry. I'm just not--

128
00:04:46,018 --> 00:04:47,555
Okay, beautiful,
you and your brain

129
00:04:47,588 --> 00:04:49,188
are coming with me, Mister.

130
00:04:49,222 --> 00:04:50,957
Oh, don't hurt
my brain, please.

131
00:04:50,990 --> 00:04:52,092
Everything's nice
and comfortable.

132
00:04:52,125 --> 00:04:53,827
Everybody's okay.

133
00:04:53,860 --> 00:04:55,862
(Observer winces)
Just keep coming with me.

134
00:04:55,895 --> 00:04:57,765
Come on Bobo, we're
getting off this planet.

135
00:04:57,798 --> 00:04:59,198
Wouldn't it be
more polite to wait

136
00:04:59,232 --> 00:05:00,533
- until after I'm dissected?
- Shut up!

137
00:05:00,567 --> 00:05:02,035
- Okay.
- You put down that thing!

138
00:05:02,068 --> 00:05:03,003
I'm not putting down that!

139
00:05:03,037 --> 00:05:07,140
(all shout at once)

140
00:05:07,173 --> 00:05:08,642
Mike, I accidentally lied.

141
00:05:08,675 --> 00:05:10,510
Your movie today
is She Creature.

142
00:05:10,543 --> 00:05:11,912
I'm not putting down the thing!

143
00:05:11,945 --> 00:05:12,480
Just watch me!

144
00:05:12,513 --> 00:05:16,017
(all shout at once)

145
00:05:16,050 --> 00:05:17,450
She Creature? (scoffs)

146
00:05:17,483 --> 00:05:19,853
You know who I'm thinking
is a she creature? Huh?

147
00:05:19,887 --> 00:05:20,788
- Yeah?
- Huh?

148
00:05:20,822 --> 00:05:21,088
- Yeah?
- Huh?

149
00:05:21,122 --> 00:05:22,288
Yeah?

150
00:05:22,322 --> 00:05:23,723
Hey, I tried to steer
us away from the planet,

151
00:05:23,757 --> 00:05:27,227
but the stupid smart guys have
cut our navigational system.

152
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:28,728
Well, maybe the
nanites can take care

153
00:05:28,762 --> 00:05:30,430
- of that little problem, huh?
- Yeah.

154
00:05:30,463 --> 00:05:32,032
We'll fix your little
problem for you, uh-huh.

155
00:05:32,065 --> 00:05:34,768
Hey Steve, Mr. Nelson
wants a number seven, pronto.

156
00:05:34,802 --> 00:05:36,603
Well there you
go, that took care...

157
00:05:36,637 --> 00:05:37,972
Hey, what's a
number seven anyway?

158
00:05:38,005 --> 00:05:38,938
(explosion)

159
00:05:38,972 --> 00:05:42,675
(all shout)

160
00:05:42,708 --> 00:05:44,445
Mike, you blew
up another planet.

161
00:05:44,478 --> 00:05:45,678
What is your deal?

162
00:05:45,712 --> 00:05:47,915
I just told them to take
care of a little problem.

163
00:05:47,948 --> 00:05:48,915
And they did.

164
00:05:48,948 --> 00:05:51,418
"Here comes Mike.
Destroyer of worlds."

165
00:05:51,452 --> 00:05:54,122
Oh god of fire and
vengeance. Stay away from me.

166
00:05:54,155 --> 00:05:55,322
Get away from me.

167
00:05:55,355 --> 00:05:57,692
(buzzer)
We got movie sign.

168
00:05:57,725 --> 00:06:02,430
(rumbling, clicking and beeping)

169
00:06:10,603 --> 00:06:12,905
- Planet killer.
- I didn't. It's not me.

170
00:06:12,938 --> 00:06:15,877
This is as colorful as
the movie's going to get.

171
00:06:15,910 --> 00:06:17,945
Ah, The RuPaul Story.

172
00:06:17,978 --> 00:06:20,813
(1950s horror film music)

173
00:06:20,847 --> 00:06:23,852
Hey, Tim Conway as Dorf
is going to be in this.

174
00:06:25,185 --> 00:06:26,987
Hey, there's Tim Finn.

175
00:06:27,020 --> 00:06:29,890
There's Gil Hodges.
There's Gil Gerard.

176
00:06:29,923 --> 00:06:33,093
There goes Joe Pesci.
There's Prunella Scales.

177
00:06:33,127 --> 00:06:35,295
There's Abe Vigoda.

178
00:06:35,328 --> 00:06:37,297
Is there a sturgeon
in the house?

179
00:06:37,330 --> 00:06:40,833
Can I borrow a fin?

180
00:06:40,867 --> 00:06:45,238
- Sea turtle.
- Yes, I do (laughs)

181
00:06:45,272 --> 00:06:46,240
"Based on drunken comments

182
00:06:46,273 --> 00:06:48,942
"made one night by Lou Rusoff."

183
00:06:48,975 --> 00:06:50,577
At least the
production was supervised.

184
00:06:50,610 --> 00:06:52,078
Things didn't get out of hand.

185
00:06:52,112 --> 00:06:55,215
Clearly the ocean does
not have metered ramps.

186
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:58,052
"Oh, it's humid today. Oof."

187
00:06:58,085 --> 00:07:02,622
(lightning sound effect)
Lee Trevino goes fishing.

188
00:07:02,655 --> 00:07:04,992
(scoffs) Samuel Z. Dunkoff.

189
00:07:05,025 --> 00:07:06,727
Yeah, Samuel Z. Wienerhead.

190
00:07:06,760 --> 00:07:09,863
Well, I think ideally it
should be related to his name.

191
00:07:09,897 --> 00:07:11,063
Oh.

192
00:07:11,097 --> 00:07:13,933
Hey, there's Bennett
Cerf, and Billy Ocean!

193
00:07:13,967 --> 00:07:15,770
Stop it, Servo.

194
00:07:16,770 --> 00:07:19,405
Once again folks, a
Golden State Production.

195
00:07:19,438 --> 00:07:20,973
Is this a
Show-Me-State Production?

196
00:07:21,007 --> 00:07:23,577
No, I think it's a
Golden State Production.

197
00:07:23,610 --> 00:07:27,847
Wait a minute, wasn't it
already produced by someone?

198
00:07:27,880 --> 00:07:29,515
Edward Cahn, Edward
Cahn, let me rock it.

199
00:07:29,548 --> 00:07:31,318
That's all I wanna do.
Edward Cahn, let me rock you.

200
00:07:31,352 --> 00:07:33,220
That's all I want to do.

201
00:07:38,225 --> 00:07:40,760
Gidget meets Magritte.

202
00:07:40,793 --> 00:07:42,662
Now, on this very
night, I have called out

203
00:07:42,695 --> 00:07:44,932
from the unknown
depths of time itself.

204
00:07:44,965 --> 00:07:48,602
- Uh-huh, and you are?
- And she is here.

205
00:07:48,635 --> 00:07:52,672
And with her coming, the
world will never be as it was.

206
00:07:52,705 --> 00:07:54,975
Neither man nor animal
will be the same.

207
00:07:55,008 --> 00:07:55,808
Nor manimal.

208
00:07:55,842 --> 00:07:58,678
This, I, Dr. Carlo Lombardi,

209
00:07:58,712 --> 00:08:00,547
have brought into being.

210
00:08:00,580 --> 00:08:03,217
Dr. Carlo Lombardi of Yonkers.

211
00:08:03,250 --> 00:08:06,853
(dog barks)

212
00:08:07,587 --> 00:08:10,357
And I, Dr. Woof Woof Lombardi.

213
00:08:10,390 --> 00:08:13,793
Well, I can certainly
see how, sleep!

214
00:08:13,827 --> 00:08:16,663
"I need my worm
medicine. I need it now."

215
00:08:16,697 --> 00:08:19,733
"What's that? Grandpa
Lombardi fell down a well?"

216
00:08:19,767 --> 00:08:21,235
"I'm sorry, Mr. Lombardi.

217
00:08:21,268 --> 00:08:22,735
"I mistook you for someone else.

218
00:08:22,768 --> 00:08:25,638
"I know my family
owes you a lot."

219
00:08:25,672 --> 00:08:26,607
"Look, you smell like spam.

220
00:08:26,640 --> 00:08:28,542
"It was my mistake, my mistake."

221
00:08:28,575 --> 00:08:30,877
"God, I hate cats."

222
00:08:30,910 --> 00:08:34,248
"I left a present for you
in the front seat of your car."

223
00:08:36,217 --> 00:08:38,852
"Top breeder, Bat Masterson."

224
00:08:38,885 --> 00:08:42,188
Hmm, Howard
the Duck was here.

225
00:08:42,222 --> 00:08:44,892
"I've got sand in my Derby."

226
00:08:47,793 --> 00:08:49,563
(flatly) "Hey,
hey, I'm the Monkee.

227
00:08:49,597 --> 00:08:52,065
"People say I monkey around."

228
00:08:53,533 --> 00:08:55,835
(faux laughs) Fun times
at the Kennedy compound.

229
00:08:55,868 --> 00:08:58,405
"Here you go,
Mr. Trafficante."

230
00:08:58,438 --> 00:09:00,407
Enjoying your weekend
with the idle rich?

231
00:09:00,440 --> 00:09:01,742
"When does it start?"

232
00:09:01,775 --> 00:09:04,443
Pretty heady stuff for a
professor of psychic research.

233
00:09:04,477 --> 00:09:05,980
You sound a
little disapproving.

234
00:09:06,013 --> 00:09:06,947
Not at all.

235
00:09:06,980 --> 00:09:08,548
I just don't feel
I belong in a world

236
00:09:08,582 --> 00:09:10,550
of yachts and racing stakes.

237
00:09:10,583 --> 00:09:12,052
What the?

238
00:09:12,085 --> 00:09:13,453
Hello?

239
00:09:13,487 --> 00:09:15,288
Including your father.
Kind of frightens me.

240
00:09:15,322 --> 00:09:16,523
Oh come now,
this type of life

241
00:09:16,557 --> 00:09:18,425
shouldn't be too
hard to get used to.

242
00:09:18,458 --> 00:09:19,627
Let's face it.

243
00:09:19,660 --> 00:09:20,793
I'm an Alloway farm boy

244
00:09:20,827 --> 00:09:23,097
with a professorship
at the university.

245
00:09:23,130 --> 00:09:25,565
But basically, a farm boy.

246
00:09:25,598 --> 00:09:27,635
I don't belong in all that.

247
00:09:27,668 --> 00:09:28,768
Very well, then.

248
00:09:28,802 --> 00:09:30,537
We'll get you away
from them for a while.

249
00:09:30,570 --> 00:09:32,772
A walk along the ocean'll do it.

250
00:09:32,805 --> 00:09:34,673
- I’d like that.
- “But I don't know how."

251
00:09:34,707 --> 00:09:38,145
I don't know how your
fiance will react to that idea.

252
00:09:38,178 --> 00:09:40,747
Oh, Bob, my ex-fiance?

253
00:09:40,780 --> 00:09:42,248
That makes quite a difference.

254
00:09:42,282 --> 00:09:44,252
- Come on, Ted.
