506
00:19:28,835 --> 00:19:29,735
You'll remember nothing.

507
00:19:29,768 --> 00:19:31,203
“You’ll remember
how to go potty

508
00:19:31,237 --> 00:19:33,407
"and chew and stuff, but..."

509
00:19:34,340 --> 00:19:37,008
He's like an
unattractive Slim Whitman.

510
00:19:37,042 --> 00:19:38,577
"That's great, Mesmer,
but you left jelly

511
00:19:38,610 --> 00:19:40,545
"all over the cutting
board this morning."

512
00:19:40,578 --> 00:19:43,917
"I've got to go levitate
over to Denny's for my shift."

513
00:19:43,950 --> 00:19:45,785
What time is it?

514
00:19:45,818 --> 00:19:46,953
Shortly after midnight.

515
00:19:46,987 --> 00:19:49,355
Don't let it all
hang down, please.

516
00:19:49,388 --> 00:19:50,957
You've had me
in a deep hypnosis

517
00:19:50,990 --> 00:19:53,192
for more than an hour.

518
00:19:53,225 --> 00:19:55,695
I asked you not to do that.

519
00:19:55,728 --> 00:19:58,898
Well, you were tired.
You needed the rest.

520
00:19:58,932 --> 00:20:00,065
(Servo mimes kiss)

521
00:20:00,098 --> 00:20:02,768
I need to get away from here.

522
00:20:02,802 --> 00:20:04,270
Away from you.

523
00:20:04,303 --> 00:20:06,138
"Uh, can I come?"

524
00:20:06,172 --> 00:20:08,542
I hate this place.

525
00:20:08,575 --> 00:20:10,877
I hate the sound of the ocean.

526
00:20:11,845 --> 00:20:13,378
I hate you.

527
00:20:13,412 --> 00:20:17,183
"I can't help but feel
that was directed at me."

528
00:20:17,217 --> 00:20:20,553
"I didn't mean I
hate you in a bad way."

529
00:20:21,587 --> 00:20:24,958
"Anyone call
about the charger?"

530
00:20:25,992 --> 00:20:27,860
You'll never leave me.

531
00:20:27,893 --> 00:20:29,495
You can't.

532
00:20:29,528 --> 00:20:30,897
I will.

533
00:20:30,930 --> 00:20:32,732
Someday I will.

534
00:20:32,765 --> 00:20:33,967
Soon.

535
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,367
"You want to
make some nachos?"

536
00:20:35,400 --> 00:20:37,503
As long as I'm
alive I'll possess you.

537
00:20:37,537 --> 00:20:39,005
"I should bag those leaves."

538
00:20:39,038 --> 00:20:40,173
There's something
beyond yourself

539
00:20:40,207 --> 00:20:42,542
that makes you need me.

540
00:20:42,575 --> 00:20:44,410
You've taken my
soul away from me.

541
00:20:44,443 --> 00:20:47,980
"You told me to take it
so you wouldn't overuse it."

542
00:20:48,013 --> 00:20:49,917
(knock on door)

543
00:20:50,983 --> 00:20:54,253
The door is open. Come in.

544
00:20:55,388 --> 00:20:58,525
"Can we get two
seats together?"

545
00:20:58,558 --> 00:20:59,793
"Hi, Max."

546
00:21:00,727 --> 00:21:02,662
"May I suggest a
size up from that?"

547
00:21:02,695 --> 00:21:05,665
- Yeah.
- I’m Lieutenant James.

548
00:21:05,698 --> 00:21:06,800
Hello.

549
00:21:06,833 --> 00:21:08,768
"This is Timmy."

550
00:21:10,770 --> 00:21:13,507
- Dr. Erickson?
- “Umm, breast?"

551
00:21:13,540 --> 00:21:14,507
Uh, yeah?

552
00:21:14,540 --> 00:21:15,742
Is this the man
you saw coming out of

553
00:21:15,775 --> 00:21:17,277
- the Jefferson house?
- “Boobies, exactly."

554
00:21:17,310 --> 00:21:19,880
- Yeah.
- No doubt in your mind?

555
00:21:19,913 --> 00:21:20,980
No.

556
00:21:21,013 --> 00:21:22,782
He knows me quite well.

557
00:21:22,815 --> 00:21:25,550
I've been trying to interest
him in my work for some time.

558
00:21:25,583 --> 00:21:27,153
You don't deny you were
in the Jefferson house

559
00:21:27,187 --> 00:21:29,888
approximately 15
minutes after 11?

560
00:21:29,922 --> 00:21:31,057
Not at all.

561
00:21:31,090 --> 00:21:32,625
Well, that closes
the investigation.

562
00:21:32,658 --> 00:21:35,195
I won't need you any
longer, doctor. Thank you.

563
00:21:35,228 --> 00:21:37,297
Nor you, miss.

564
00:21:38,397 --> 00:21:42,835
Wow, it's the federal
witness seduction program.

565
00:21:42,868 --> 00:21:44,337
"Umm, 'Sleep?' "

566
00:21:44,370 --> 00:21:45,805
" 'Sleep?' "

567
00:21:47,373 --> 00:21:48,607
"You want to
go home and play?

568
00:21:48,640 --> 00:21:50,910
- “I got a box of men."
- What's it all about?

569
00:21:52,412 --> 00:21:55,115
Maybe we can talk about
it over a cup of coffee.

570
00:21:55,148 --> 00:21:56,548
I'd like that.

571
00:21:56,582 --> 00:21:59,185
"Would you like a C-cup
or a D-cup of coffee?"

572
00:21:59,218 --> 00:22:00,853
"So, you go to
carnival locations

573
00:22:00,887 --> 00:22:02,988
"and wait for them, huh?"

574
00:22:03,022 --> 00:22:05,358
(mystical music)

575
00:22:05,392 --> 00:22:06,525
- Ooh.
- Hey.

576
00:22:06,558 --> 00:22:09,495
"Look into my oily T-zone."

577
00:22:09,528 --> 00:22:10,530
I can't go with you.

578
00:22:10,563 --> 00:22:12,332
"I'm not a coffee achiever."

579
00:22:13,800 --> 00:22:16,202
And he ducks
out of the screen.

580
00:22:16,235 --> 00:22:17,670
(Servo laughs)
Bye.

581
00:22:17,703 --> 00:22:20,140
"Guess the stain
and win a prize."

582
00:22:20,173 --> 00:22:21,773
Oh.

583
00:22:21,807 --> 00:22:23,308
You say you
knew they were dead

584
00:22:23,342 --> 00:22:25,243
the minute you
saw the open door.

585
00:22:25,277 --> 00:22:27,513
- “Yeah, see?"
- Yes, pity.

586
00:22:27,547 --> 00:22:29,648
Nice young couple.

587
00:22:29,682 --> 00:22:32,418
She came out of the ocean,
just as I said she would.

588
00:22:32,452 --> 00:22:33,585
And she'll come again.

589
00:22:33,618 --> 00:22:35,588
Look, I'm not
a paying customer.

590
00:22:35,622 --> 00:22:37,290
I'm a police officer.

591
00:22:37,323 --> 00:22:38,623
She comes from the
beginning of time.

592
00:22:38,657 --> 00:22:41,260
(they fake coughing)
Huge and indestructible.

593
00:22:41,293 --> 00:22:42,462
"Thank you."

594
00:22:42,495 --> 00:22:44,730
And I'm the force
that gives her life.

595
00:22:44,763 --> 00:22:47,167
All I know, you were seen
coming out of that house

596
00:22:47,200 --> 00:22:49,735
leaving two corpses behind you.

597
00:22:49,768 --> 00:22:51,437
And the occult world
notwithstanding,

598
00:22:51,470 --> 00:22:52,638
I think I'll take you downtown

599
00:22:52,672 --> 00:22:54,640
and wait until the
reports come in.

600
00:22:54,673 --> 00:22:56,442
I can tell you what
the reports will say.

601
00:22:56,475 --> 00:22:57,677
"They'll say
(shouts) 'Sleep.' "

602
00:22:57,710 --> 00:22:59,478
That no living
thing killed them.

603
00:22:59,512 --> 00:23:00,780
Yeah, I know.

604
00:23:00,813 --> 00:23:03,782
It was a materialization
of the prehistoric female.

605
00:23:03,815 --> 00:23:06,920
A transmigration of the
soul of a living woman,

606
00:23:06,953 --> 00:23:08,620
into her first life body.

607
00:23:08,653 --> 00:23:10,690
Save it, save
it for downtown.

608
00:23:10,723 --> 00:23:15,695
(rumbling, clicking and beeping)

609
00:23:23,068 --> 00:23:24,237
Hey Mike, there you are.

610
00:23:24,270 --> 00:23:25,738
I had an idea and I
wanted to run it by

611
00:23:25,772 --> 00:23:27,673
a totally average,
unspectacular,

612
00:23:27,707 --> 00:23:31,277
not overly-bright
consumer, and here you are.

613
00:23:31,310 --> 00:23:32,778
(faux laughter)
Yeah, sure Crow.

614
00:23:32,812 --> 00:23:35,182
Good. Hey, give me that
thing under there will you?

615
00:23:35,215 --> 00:23:36,482
Yeah. Mm-hmm.

616
00:23:36,515 --> 00:23:39,218
It's my Tickle Me
Carlo Lombardi doll.

617
00:23:39,252 --> 00:23:40,652
Oh, wow. What the?

618
00:23:40,685 --> 00:23:44,023
Yeah, it's just like the
lovable Tickle Me Elmo doll.

619
00:23:44,057 --> 00:23:47,460
- Only it's Carlo Lombardi.
- What? Why?

620
00:23:47,493 --> 00:23:49,095
Oh that's a lot
of little boys,

621
00:23:49,128 --> 00:23:50,663
and it's a reaction to dolls,

622
00:23:50,697 --> 00:23:52,832
but you'll grow to
love it as you take it

623
00:23:52,865 --> 00:23:54,667
into your room, perhaps prop it

624
00:23:54,700 --> 00:23:56,937
next to your bed as you sleep.

625
00:23:56,970 --> 00:23:58,370
He'll watch over you.

626
00:23:58,403 --> 00:24:00,638
He's Dr. Carlo Lombardi.

627
00:24:00,672 --> 00:24:04,010
- Crow, why you make a doll?
- Go ahead, Mike. Tickle him.

628
00:24:04,043 --> 00:24:04,910
No.

629
00:24:04,943 --> 00:24:06,678
Oh, I think
you'd better, Mike.

630
00:24:06,712 --> 00:24:08,247
Tickle Me Carlo Lombardi

631
00:24:08,280 --> 00:24:10,450
doesn't like to be disappointed.

632
00:24:10,483 --> 00:24:12,385
Well, just to be safe, okay.

633
00:24:12,418 --> 00:24:13,618
That's right.

634
00:24:13,652 --> 00:24:15,255
(dolls laughs)
Tickle Me Carlo Lombardi

635
00:24:15,288 --> 00:24:16,957
is your friend.

636
00:24:16,990 --> 00:24:17,990
Forever.

637
00:24:18,023 --> 00:24:20,627
(doll laughs)
Yeah, and I made him sticky

638
00:24:20,660 --> 00:24:22,395
so he's even more fun.

639
00:24:22,428 --> 00:24:23,795
(Mike strains)
You can feed him

640
00:24:23,828 --> 00:24:27,600
the special baby food
included and in a few minutes

641
00:24:27,633 --> 00:24:31,003
change Tickle Me Carlo
Lombardi's daidie.

642
00:24:31,037 --> 00:24:31,970
No, no!

643
00:24:32,003 --> 00:24:33,072
And there's a song too.

644
00:24:33,105 --> 00:24:35,808
♪ Who's that fat little
funny little doll

645
00:24:35,842 --> 00:24:38,710
♪ It's Tickle Me Carlo Lombardi

646
00:24:38,743 --> 00:24:41,380
♪ Who's little diaper
needs a good little change

647
00:24:41,413 --> 00:24:44,150
♪ It's Tickle Me
Carlo Lombardi

648
00:24:44,183 --> 00:24:45,517
Tickle Me Carlo Lombardi

649
00:24:45,550 --> 00:24:47,320
and Tickle Me Carlo
Lombardi sold separately.

650
00:24:47,353 --> 00:24:50,022
(doll laughs)
You know, that thing's

651
00:24:50,055 --> 00:24:51,523
kind of creepy.

652
00:24:51,557 --> 00:24:52,725
No, I don't think it'll work.

653
00:24:52,758 --> 00:24:54,193
You can have that
doll though, Mike.

654
00:24:54,227 --> 00:24:55,595
I'm done with it. Thank you.

655
00:24:55,628 --> 00:24:58,163
(doll laughs)

656
00:24:59,632 --> 00:25:04,203
(light music)

657
00:25:05,705 --> 00:25:06,905
Huh, will you look at that?

658
00:25:06,938 --> 00:25:09,675
Despite all his money,
Mr. Drysdale eats alone.

659
00:25:09,708 --> 00:25:11,377
"Where's my shirred eggs?"

660
00:25:11,410 --> 00:25:14,147
(dog barks)

661
00:25:14,180 --> 00:25:15,648
"Works every time."

662
00:25:15,682 --> 00:25:18,483
That dog, it
gives me the jitters.

663
00:25:18,517 --> 00:25:19,785
I get a nervous Adam's apple,

664
00:25:19,818 --> 00:25:21,653
and that makes my tie unfold.

665
00:25:21,687 --> 00:25:22,755
Inspired by Balki.

666
00:25:22,788 --> 00:25:24,757
- Morning, gentlemen.
- Morning, Ted.

667
00:25:24,790 --> 00:25:26,192
Dorothy will be
down in a minute.

668
00:25:26,225 --> 00:25:28,293
"Dorothy can't.
I killed her."

669
00:25:28,327 --> 00:25:29,228
I'm certainly not too popular

670
00:25:29,262 --> 00:25:31,930
with that member of your family.

671
00:25:31,963 --> 00:25:33,498
Take him to the
kitchen and get him

672
00:25:33,532 --> 00:25:34,967
- something to eat, huh?
- The last time I took him

673
00:25:35,000 --> 00:25:37,703
to the kitchen, he
nearly had the cook.

674
00:25:37,737 --> 00:25:39,572
"Thank you very
much. Was so stupid."

675
00:25:39,605 --> 00:25:40,373
Come on, dog.

676
00:25:40,407 --> 00:25:42,107
(dog growls and barks)

677
00:25:42,140 --> 00:25:45,612
"Oh god, I am dead.
My carotid artery."

678
00:25:45,645 --> 00:25:47,713
"Racket's really
heavy today."

679
00:25:47,747 --> 00:25:48,982
Carnelli arrives at 10.

680
00:25:49,015 --> 00:25:51,450
Good. Makes your
men get up early.

681
00:25:51,483 --> 00:25:53,285
Shows he's aggressive,
wants to get ahead.

682
00:25:53,318 --> 00:25:54,487
"Damn Jerries at it again."

683
00:25:54,520 --> 00:25:56,788
You give me too much
credit, Mr. Chappel.

684
00:25:56,822 --> 00:26:00,458
This Jefferson thing
last night, pretty grim.

685
00:26:00,492 --> 00:26:01,860
Kept them all
buzzing for a while

686
00:26:01,893 --> 00:26:04,730
- after Dorothy came home.
- “I’m over here, sir."

687
00:26:04,763 --> 00:26:05,998
It's surprising
how many of them

688
00:26:06,032 --> 00:26:08,733
think that Lombardi had
something to do with it.

689
00:26:08,767 --> 00:26:10,702
The whole gang's been
down to see his show.

690
00:26:10,735 --> 00:26:12,672
- “Sorry, looked at you."
- Chappel tried to bully me

691
00:26:12,705 --> 00:26:15,075
- into going along.
- “Damn wigwags."

692
00:26:16,875 --> 00:26:18,677
Take a look at
that front page.

693
00:26:18,710 --> 00:26:21,113
"God ailing, still holds on."

694
00:26:21,147 --> 00:26:24,217
"Let me get my
welding glasses on here."

695
00:26:26,885 --> 00:26:28,253
I play a little
game every morning.

696
00:26:28,287 --> 00:26:31,123
- I call it my front page game.
- “Sure you do."

697
00:26:31,157 --> 00:26:34,193
I'm getting a little old
to play most of the others.

698
00:26:34,227 --> 00:26:35,962
"I'm a limp noodle."

699
00:26:35,995 --> 00:26:37,563
I read the front
page every morning

700
00:26:37,597 --> 00:26:39,298
and see if I can pick
out an item or two

701
00:26:39,332 --> 00:26:40,867
that will make me
a lot of money.

702
00:26:40,900 --> 00:26:43,535
Surprising how often
it's worked out.

703
00:26:43,568 --> 00:26:44,803
You ever try it?

704
00:26:44,837 --> 00:26:46,438
No, I can't say I have.

705
00:26:46,472 --> 00:26:48,440
Can the She Creature
begin killing now?

706
00:26:48,473 --> 00:26:50,410
You read about
the Jefferson murder?

707
00:26:50,443 --> 00:26:51,677
Yes.

708
00:26:51,710 --> 00:26:54,213
There's a million
dollar idea in that.

709
00:26:54,247 --> 00:26:56,115
Last paragraph. Read it.

710
00:26:56,148 --> 00:26:59,752
"Sell something for
a million dollars."

711
00:26:59,785 --> 00:27:01,420
"One baffling
aspect of the case

712
00:27:01,453 --> 00:27:03,688
"concerns Dr. Carlo Lombardi,

713
00:27:03,722 --> 00:27:06,158
"carnival hypnotist
and prognosticator."

714
00:27:06,192 --> 00:27:07,793
- That's the plot summary.
- “Only last week,

715
00:27:07,827 --> 00:27:10,028
"he predicted that such a
murder would take place,

716
00:27:10,062 --> 00:27:12,698
"describing it with
grizzly accuracy.

717
00:27:12,732 --> 00:27:14,967
"He was questioned by the
police, but not held."

718
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:16,868
"Molly Ivins can't say that."

719
00:27:16,902 --> 00:27:19,305
You see a fortune in that?

720
00:27:19,338 --> 00:27:20,973
- Yes.
- “Oh, wait. No."

721
00:27:21,007 --> 00:27:22,542
Yes, and it's
right up your alley.

722
00:27:22,575 --> 00:27:23,708
Ouch.

723
00:27:23,742 --> 00:27:25,443
And yours is a
wedding present.

724
00:27:25,477 --> 00:27:26,778
You're serious, aren't you?

725
00:27:26,812 --> 00:27:28,047
Couldn't be more so.

726
00:27:28,080 --> 00:27:30,815
We'll take this two-bit
local sideshow man

727
00:27:30,848 --> 00:27:33,185
and build him into the
biggest thing in the country.

728
00:27:33,218 --> 00:27:36,255
Build him up until his
name's on everyone's lips.

729
00:27:36,288 --> 00:27:37,723
Lombardi books.

730
00:27:37,757 --> 00:27:40,727
Syndicated columns,
lectures, television shows.

731
00:27:40,760 --> 00:27:41,993
"Cheese, a line
of underwear."

732
00:27:42,027 --> 00:27:43,828
This prediction of his
is worth a million dollars

733
00:27:43,862 --> 00:27:46,765
- and you and I can do it.
- Where do I fit in?

734
00:27:46,798 --> 00:27:48,867
"You don't. I bought
you out already."

735
00:27:48,900 --> 00:27:50,702
You can give him the
stamp of authenticity.

736
00:27:50,735 --> 00:27:52,705
(Crow mimics his accent)
"Dr. Erickson,

737
00:27:52,738 --> 00:27:54,640
"psychic research
specialist says

738
00:27:54,673 --> 00:27:56,442
"Lombardi experiments amazing.

739
00:27:56,475 --> 00:27:58,943
"Open new avenues in
the understanding of
the subconscious."

740
00:27:58,977 --> 00:28:02,648
Why don't you kiss him
instead of talking him to death?

741
00:28:02,682 --> 00:28:04,483
They'll swallow it, and
they'll swallow it whole

742
00:28:04,517 --> 00:28:05,883
- and love it.
- “Yes."

743
00:28:05,917 --> 00:28:08,988
This is the sort of escape
stuff the world's crying for.

744
00:28:09,022 --> 00:28:10,688
Look at my wife and her friends.

745
00:28:10,722 --> 00:28:13,292
- “No thanks."
- It’s a natural.

746
00:28:13,325 --> 00:28:14,293
It'll be a lot for me,

747
00:28:14,327 --> 00:28:16,695
and money for you and Dorothy.

748
00:28:16,728 --> 00:28:18,830
I've been trained to fight
stupidity and ignorance,

749
00:28:18,863 --> 00:28:20,832
- not get rich on it.
- “So put 'em up!"

750
00:28:20,865 --> 00:28:23,870
A man like Lombardi put
hypnosis back 25 years.

751
00:28:23,903 --> 00:28:25,703
"Ever prune your ferns?"

752
00:28:25,737 --> 00:28:27,607
They've taken a
modern tool of science

753
00:28:27,640 --> 00:28:29,775
and made a plaything out of it.

754
00:28:29,808 --> 00:28:31,177
Worse than that, a weapon,

755
00:28:31,210 --> 00:28:33,378
and in the hands of
quacks like Lombardi...

756
00:28:33,412 --> 00:28:36,148
- Quack.
- A dangerous weapon.

757
00:28:36,182 --> 00:28:38,750
And you want me to help
sell him to the public?

