into the house for a sherry.

2245
01:23:53,062 --> 01:23:54,730
"We'll have a little chinwag."

2246
01:23:55,832 --> 01:23:58,167
Meanwhile, in a
nearby wedding cake.

2247
01:23:59,168 --> 01:24:01,470
"I want those
Glengarry leads."

2248
01:24:02,772 --> 01:24:04,540
General Tom Thumb.

2249
01:24:08,143 --> 01:24:09,278
Wait a minute,
how did he get?

2250
01:24:09,312 --> 01:24:12,513
- Foul.
- Illegal procedure.

2251
01:24:12,547 --> 01:24:14,017
Looks like my grandma
framed this shot.

2252
01:24:14,050 --> 01:24:15,017
Plenty of wall.

2253
01:24:15,050 --> 01:24:16,652
(Creature grunts)

2254
01:24:16,685 --> 01:24:18,788
Now do you believe, doctor?

2255
01:24:18,822 --> 01:24:20,423
Kill it!

2256
01:24:20,923 --> 01:24:22,358
"No."

2257
01:24:23,592 --> 01:24:25,427
"Wait a minute. You're
not Roy Johnson are you?

2258
01:24:25,460 --> 01:24:28,832
"I'm supposed to
kill Roy Johnson."

2259
01:24:28,865 --> 01:24:30,600
"No. Bad.

2260
01:24:30,633 --> 01:24:32,202
"No. No."

2261
01:24:33,835 --> 01:24:36,672
"Well, mm, gosh,
I, mm, hmm. Uh."

2262
01:24:38,040 --> 01:24:39,308
And now she's just
pretending to be hypnotized

2263
01:24:39,342 --> 01:24:41,778
so she doesn't have to help.

2264
01:24:43,078 --> 01:24:45,080
"Okay, girlfriend,
I got the Haagen-Dazs.

2265
01:24:45,113 --> 01:24:46,817
"Let's dish."

2266
01:24:49,018 --> 01:24:51,253
Fear? Elation? What is it?

2267
01:24:51,287 --> 01:24:52,220
"And he said he
was going to call

2268
01:24:52,253 --> 01:24:54,290
"but then he doesn't call."

2269
01:24:54,323 --> 01:24:55,457
Makes you wonder what

2270
01:24:55,490 --> 01:24:57,827
the He Creature
would look like, huh?

2271
01:24:58,960 --> 01:25:02,232
Despair? Love? Joy? Tell us!

2272
01:25:03,398 --> 01:25:06,235
Man, she's got a
prison matron bosom.

2273
01:25:06,268 --> 01:25:07,435
Eww, I think the director

2274
01:25:07,468 --> 01:25:09,272
had some issues with
his mother or something.

2275
01:25:09,305 --> 01:25:12,073
(Servo sobs)
Concern? Passion?

2276
01:25:12,107 --> 01:25:14,477
Hunger? What, Lance?

2277
01:25:15,677 --> 01:25:18,113
"Ah, she's got a
slight mustache problem."

2278
01:25:18,147 --> 01:25:20,883
You know, you can
overcondition your hair.

2279
01:25:25,922 --> 01:25:29,292
Ennui? Angst? Apathy? Gas?

2280
01:25:29,325 --> 01:25:31,427
Self-delivering cotton candy.

2281
01:25:31,460 --> 01:25:34,397
It's the She Vicks
VapoRub Creature.

2282
01:25:35,998 --> 01:25:37,565
"Well, cut the
downdraft there.

2283
01:25:37,598 --> 01:25:39,935
"Ooh, back, back! I want
to go the other way!

2284
01:25:39,968 --> 01:25:41,337
"Damn."

2285
01:25:42,237 --> 01:25:46,042
Cold? Jubilant? Headachey?

2286
01:25:46,075 --> 01:25:49,278
His emotional memory
is the previous scene.

2287
01:25:51,080 --> 01:25:54,083
"Oh, I ate too
much chocolate.

2288
01:25:54,117 --> 01:25:55,952
"Oh, oh."

2289
01:25:55,985 --> 01:25:59,120
"Do I have
anything on my face?"

2290
01:25:59,153 --> 01:26:00,990
You couldn't kill
the man you loved.

2291
01:26:01,023 --> 01:26:03,625
"Hair styled by Elmarco."

2292
01:26:03,658 --> 01:26:06,162
I mustn't let you die.

2293
01:26:06,195 --> 01:26:07,595
Your beauty must live.

2294
01:26:07,628 --> 01:26:10,898
"Your average
attractiveness must live on."

2295
01:26:10,932 --> 01:26:13,768
I will touch you
and you will awaken.

2296
01:26:13,802 --> 01:26:15,872
Young and beautiful.

2297
01:26:15,905 --> 01:26:17,707
Freed forever from the past.

2298
01:26:17,740 --> 01:26:20,008
Man, he shouldn't
have siphoned motor oil.

2299
01:26:20,042 --> 01:26:22,912
What I have done,
no man can ever do.

2300
01:26:22,945 --> 01:26:25,480
Take such a lame act so far.

2301
01:26:25,513 --> 01:26:28,083
- “And, I'm dead."
- “Thank you."

2302
01:26:28,117 --> 01:26:30,018
Ah, it's working perfectly.

2303
01:26:30,052 --> 01:26:32,522
(menacing music)

2304
01:26:34,390 --> 01:26:36,558
Ah, Frodo's going snorkeling.

2305
01:26:39,228 --> 01:26:40,863
There. Fire.

2306
01:26:40,897 --> 01:26:42,097
I can't see anything.

2307
01:26:42,130 --> 01:26:44,200
Where I'm pointing
at. Hurry up.

2308
01:26:44,233 --> 01:26:46,602
"Okay, civilian."

2309
01:26:46,635 --> 01:26:49,672
Hey, it does
seem to be helping.

2310
01:26:49,705 --> 01:26:51,673
- I don't see anything.
- Fire!

2311
01:26:51,707 --> 01:26:53,075
Maybe they should
have a staff meeting

2312
01:26:53,108 --> 01:26:55,812
about letting citizens
boss them around.

2313
01:26:57,112 --> 01:26:59,748
- You see anything?
- No.

2314
01:26:59,782 --> 01:27:01,217
How about you, doc?

2315
01:27:01,250 --> 01:27:03,685
Can you still see something?

2316
01:27:03,718 --> 01:27:04,953
No.

2317
01:27:04,987 --> 01:27:06,288
I was mistaken.

2318
01:27:06,322 --> 01:27:07,688
(Servo laughs)

2319
01:27:07,722 --> 01:27:10,058
"Who was that lethargic
lunkheaded stranger?"

2320
01:27:10,092 --> 01:27:11,760
"I don't know."

2321
01:27:11,793 --> 01:27:12,628
"I'm sorry I touched you,

2322
01:27:12,662 --> 01:27:14,630
"but you don't have
to become a nun."

2323
01:27:14,663 --> 01:27:17,500
- She was here, wasn't she?
- “I smell Tabu."

2324
01:27:17,533 --> 01:27:18,733
Yes.

2325
01:27:18,767 --> 01:27:21,170
(flatly) "Wow, look at
those worms down there."

2326
01:27:21,203 --> 01:27:22,972
He's got a list of
his facial expressions

2327
01:27:23,005 --> 01:27:25,340
taped to her back.

2328
01:27:25,373 --> 01:27:28,443
She killed Carlo.

2329
01:27:28,477 --> 01:27:30,112
He forced her to
come out of the world.

2330
01:27:30,145 --> 01:27:31,613
He should go back to her own.

2331
01:27:31,647 --> 01:27:32,613
Huh?

2332
01:27:32,647 --> 01:27:33,782
There are a lot
of dark corners

2333
01:27:33,815 --> 01:27:35,750
we weren't meant to
pry into, I guess.

2334
01:27:35,783 --> 01:27:37,920
"Are you saying you
still haven't showered?"

2335
01:27:39,788 --> 01:27:44,092
"Uh, are we
moving over here now?

2336
01:27:44,125 --> 01:27:46,828
"I'm right here if you need me."

2337
01:27:47,628 --> 01:27:51,433
She'll never
be back, will she?

2338
01:27:51,467 --> 01:27:52,433
No.

2339
01:27:52,467 --> 01:27:55,538
"And you'll never
be back either, right?"

2340
01:27:56,872 --> 01:27:58,473
And the Mysterians.

2341
01:27:58,507 --> 01:28:00,308
Man, if I ever
wanted to put a movie

2342
01:28:00,342 --> 01:28:02,978
into a stump grinder
this is the one.

2343
01:28:03,012 --> 01:28:04,413
- Yeah, me too.
- Man.

2344
01:28:04,447 --> 01:28:09,618
(rumbling, clicking and beeping)

2345
01:28:15,590 --> 01:28:16,792
So guys, what do you make of

2346
01:28:16,825 --> 01:28:18,160
that big question mark
at the end of the movie?

2347
01:28:18,193 --> 01:28:19,828
Well, I think they
were asking when,

2348
01:28:19,862 --> 01:28:23,465
as in, when will
this movie not exist?

2349
01:28:23,498 --> 01:28:25,200
Or, maybe it
was a why question,

2350
01:28:25,233 --> 01:28:27,302
as in, why did King
George and his parliament

2351
01:28:27,335 --> 01:28:29,538
react with such
indifference, nay arrogance,

2352
01:28:29,572 --> 01:28:31,140
to the colonists'
longstanding grievances

2353
01:28:31,173 --> 01:28:32,940
of taxation without
representation

2354
01:28:32,973 --> 01:28:35,710
leading to the Revolution
which led to the United States

2355
01:28:35,743 --> 01:28:38,313
which led to California
which led to Hollywood

2356
01:28:38,347 --> 01:28:39,748
and the motion picture
industry which led

2357
01:28:39,782 --> 01:28:43,418
ultimately to this hard,
bitter little nut of a movie.

2358
01:28:43,452 --> 01:28:44,620
It's a good point.

2359
01:28:44,653 --> 01:28:46,688
But I think it may have
been a hmm question,

2360
01:28:46,722 --> 01:28:48,923
as in, "Hmm? I'm sorry,
I didn't hear you.

2361
01:28:48,957 --> 01:28:51,760
"This crappy movie was
sitting on my head."

2362
01:28:51,793 --> 01:28:53,062
Hey say, guys,
it just hit me.

2363
01:28:53,095 --> 01:28:54,495
We're free to escape!

2364
01:28:54,528 --> 01:28:56,732
Since Mike blew up
the Observers' planet.

2365
01:28:56,765 --> 01:28:58,067
- I didn't. I mean, I asked--
- Right, and Mrs. Forrester

2366
01:28:58,100 --> 01:29:00,502
and the Brain Guy seem to
be tied up looking for Bobo.

2367
01:29:00,535 --> 01:29:02,503
- Yeah, let's boogie!
- Woohoo!

2368
01:29:02,537 --> 01:29:03,738
Okay, well, here we go.

2369
01:29:03,772 --> 01:29:06,442
- To infinity and--
- Shh! Disney. Lawsuit.

2370
01:29:06,475 --> 01:29:08,010
- Some other places!
- Yeah.

2371
01:29:08,043 --> 01:29:09,177
(engine coughs)
Hmm.

2372
01:29:09,210 --> 01:29:10,412
Doesn't seem to be turning over.

2373
01:29:10,445 --> 01:29:12,180
I wonder what's going on.

2374
01:29:12,213 --> 01:29:13,582
What's going on?

2375
01:29:13,615 --> 01:29:17,352
We got it goin' on, that's
what's going on, huh?

2376
01:29:17,385 --> 01:29:20,122
How about this guy here, huh?

2377
01:29:20,155 --> 01:29:22,657
I say, "Hmm, I sure would hate

2378
01:29:22,690 --> 01:29:25,493
"for those eight balls on
the satellite to escape."

2379
01:29:25,527 --> 01:29:28,863
This beautiful man
right here says,

2380
01:29:28,897 --> 01:29:29,832
"Let me handle it."

2381
01:29:29,865 --> 01:29:35,037
He is holding you here
with his mi-i-ind.

2382
01:29:35,070 --> 01:29:38,507
You poor dumb schmucks.
How do you like that?

2383
01:29:38,540 --> 01:29:40,275
How'd you like to have
this guy on your crew

2384
01:29:40,308 --> 01:29:42,878
instead of those
yappy little tin cans

2385
01:29:42,912 --> 01:29:44,045
you hang out with?

2386
01:29:44,078 --> 01:29:47,782
- This guy is the best.
- Why, thank you Pearl.

2387
01:29:47,815 --> 01:29:49,718
Tell you something
else now sonny.

2388
01:29:49,752 --> 01:29:51,653
This guy's gunnin' for you.

2389
01:29:51,687 --> 01:29:54,657
You blew up this man's wo-o-rld,

2390
01:29:54,690 --> 01:29:57,392
as I will continue to remind him

2391
01:29:57,425 --> 01:29:59,027
every chance I get.

2392
01:29:59,060 --> 01:30:00,695
You whacked his planet, man,

2393
01:30:00,728 --> 01:30:03,998
and he is plenty
cheesed, let me tell you.

2394
01:30:04,032 --> 01:30:07,635
Yes, you have destroyed
an ancient and proud race.

2395
01:30:07,668 --> 01:30:09,838
My people. And let
me tell you that I--

2396
01:30:09,872 --> 01:30:13,175
I was talking.

2397
01:30:13,208 --> 01:30:15,677
Boy, everything's
about you isn't it?

2398
01:30:15,710 --> 01:30:18,513
- I’m very sorry.
- Anyway Nelson.

2399
01:30:18,547 --> 01:30:21,950
You're mine. You'll
never escape.

2400
01:30:21,983 --> 01:30:23,085
Never!

2401
01:30:23,118 --> 01:30:28,090
(Pearl laughs maniacally)

2402
01:30:29,023 --> 01:30:30,958
Excuse me, malevolent one,

2403
01:30:30,992 --> 01:30:33,562
but hadn't we ought to
go get Professor Bobo?

2404
01:30:33,595 --> 01:30:35,563
Hmm. That's a good idea.

2405
01:30:35,597 --> 01:30:37,733
Say, could you hand
me the Cheez-Its?

2406
01:30:37,767 --> 01:30:40,668
- Why, certainly.
- Thanks.

2407
01:30:40,702 --> 01:30:44,373
(loudly) I,
give, the, orders.

2408
01:30:44,407 --> 01:30:45,507
Oh.

2409
01:30:45,540 --> 01:30:48,843
Hey, we'd better
go find Bobo.

2410
01:30:48,877 --> 01:30:53,883
(slow music)

2411
01:31:49,872 --> 01:31:51,507
Ow.

2412
01:31:52,440 --> 01:31:54,143
My spine.

2413
01:31:55,812 --> 01:31:57,513
Ow.
